attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a long spine.** Columns 0 to 27, `yggX` to `tkt`, are carried by 91 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0 to 7% of calls {S1}. The model names 85 to 99.6% of them, fewest at column 7, `hemW`, 85% {S1}.

@variable **A fork follows at `cmtB` and `cmtA`**, columns 28 and 29, carried by 89%, with a second family in 20 and 32% {S2.c28, S2.c29}. Then columns 40 to 44, `srsR` to `scpA`, are variable, carried by 80 to 88%, in a region of plasticity in 60 to 65% of calls, [[methylmalonyl-coa mutase]] {S4, Q}. The spine at columns 57 to 59, `gcvT` to `gcvP`, is [[glycine cleavage]] {S7, Q}.

@model **The model names about as many genes on the spine columns as on the fork and variable ones**, 94 against 93%, and hesitates less there, 0.26 against 0.34 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 21, `yqgD`, is a spine column, at 0.83 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on fork and variable columns.** Columns 68 to 79, `xerD` to `ghxQ`, are carried by 40 to 90%, in a region of plasticity in 4 to 83% of calls {S10}. The last column is `ghxQ`, in 40% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 94% of genes**, 0.28 bits on average, perplexity 1.4 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.69 against 0.18 bits, and names fewer genes, 85% against 96% {C}.

